			"difficulty": "Hard",
			"points": 15,
			"questionText": "Two angles of elevation to top of tree are 30° and 45° from points 20m apart. Find tree height.",
			"questionType": "multiple-choice",
			"options": [
				{ "id": "A", "text": "27.32m", "isCorrect": true },
				{ "id": "B", "text": "20m", "isCorrect": false },
				{ "id": "C", "text": "40m", "isCorrect": false },
				{ "id": "D", "text": "14.6m", "isCorrect": false }
			],
			"supportsDiagram": false,
			"diagram": null,
			"hint": "Set up two equations with same height h and solve.",
			"explanation": "Let distance to nearer point be x. h = x·tan45° = x·1 = x. Also h = (x+20)·tan30° = (x+20)/√3. So x = (x+20)/√3 gives √3x = x+20 → x(√3-1)=20 → x=20/(√3-1) ≈ 27.32. Then h = 27.32"
